#
# Conformance case: transaction/isolation-write-skew-serializable.
#
# A logic:ConcurrentComposition whose two legs form a WRITE SKEW (each leg reads a
# situation the other writes), producing a conflict-CYCLIC witnessed schedule. The
# run declares a logic:IsolationLevel (logic:declaredIsolationLevel). The concurrent
# evaluator realizes snapshot isolation, so it records logic:isolationLevelAdequacy:
# a write-skew schedule is ADEQUATE for logic:SnapshotIsolation (snapshot admits write
# skew) yet INADEQUATE for logic:SerializableIsolation (with a logic:isolationInadequacyReason).
#
# CRITICAL: the teleology evaluator seeds ONLY from input.nq world facts; this
# input.logic.ttl carries the minimal, clean-compiling, certifiable program axiom.

@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://example.org/transaction/isolation-write-skew-serializable/> .

ex:GoalExpression a logic:GoalExpression .

ex:TransactionContract a logic:ReasoningContract ;
    logic:evolution logic:TransactionPathEvolution .
